    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nPrime Town Centre commercial/residential premises - totally renovated in 2019.This turn-key building now incorporates 17 bedrooms, cafe, private lounge/meeting room, kitchen, side yard and rear carpark both with double gate access from the road. The large rear car park has the potential for further development subject to planning permission. Arus Brugha is an iconic building in the heart of the bustling coastal town of Dungarvan. Originally built circa 1880 as a hotel, the property was the former Waterford County Council building and offices until 1998.Meticulously renovated and extended into high quality accommodation and cafe by the current owner in 2019, the property has 820 sq.m of floor space over 3 floors and is a unique opportunity to purchase a turn-key building in the thriving town of Dungarvan where there is currently high demand for accommodation. For further info contact David Reynolds on 058 23444."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li>Prime town centre commercial/residential premises.</li><li>Turn-key. Totally renovated in 2019.</li><li>17 bedrooms - all ensuite.</li><li>Additional shower rooms on upper floors.</li><li>Fully certified. </li><li>Just off the main N25 Cork-Waterford route.</li><li>Sunny side yard.</li><li>Large rear car park with potential.</li><li>Fully equipped kitchen.</li><li>Mains services.</ul>"
      },
